{
  "answer": "Under the Data Processing Addendum, Personal Data may be transferred outside the European Economic Area (EEA) under the following conditions: 1. The transfer is covered by an adequacy decision from a third country or territory that has been deemed to provide an adequate level of protection for personal data compared to the EEA. 2. Appropriate safeguards are in place, such as standard contractual clauses approved by the European Commission, which ensure that the recipient country provides an equivalent level of protection for personal data.",
